This fixture is DISTRIBUTION-ONLY. It must never be copied to a consumer.

It is a MUTATION BATTERY behind the shipped fixture core/fixtures/pause-question-in-prose.
It builds sed-mutated copies of core/hooks/ai-dlc-continue.sh under mktemp, drives the shipped
fixture's own run.sh against each one, and asserts that each mutant turns exactly the named arm
red. Editing copies of core's own sources is the third shape in .claude/rules/fixture-ship-decl.md,
and a consumer running it would pay the cost of six extra hook drives per mutant for a result
about the DISTRIBUTION's hook rather than its own.

It also carries the byte-exact half of the shipped fixture's A7: the block reason on a
non-firing flag-down seed is compared byte for byte against the same hook with only the
prepend branch neutered, in both directions. That needs a mutant, which is why it lives here.

The shipped fixture is NOT vacuous without this battery. Its firing arms (F1, F2) are
PRESENCE-shaped -- each demands a specific key or a specific sentence -- so a hook replaced by
`exit 0`, or one whose arm was deleted, fails them rather than passing them silently.
